## Context

Child 6 of tracker `tickets/0240`, which owns the rationale.

R7 is per-language lanes: each language works in its own. Ticket `0037` proposes
the stronger property — an EN or FR query finding Vietnamese content. A
multilingual embedder is the mechanism for both, so the tracker's ruling is to
measure it here, while the vectors from the CPU arm are already on disk, rather
than re-running the whole campaign later.

**Division of ownership, and it matters.** `tickets/0037` owns the requirement
text, the proposed R29 and its ratification. This ticket owns only the
measurement. Do not write requirement prose here, and do not edit `0037`'s
proposal — feed it evidence.

## Relevant files

- `tickets/0240-...erg` — the tracker
- `tickets/0037-cross-lingual-retrieval-query-in-en-fr-f.erg` — owns R29 and its
  proposal; awaiting the author's ruling
- the CPU-arm vectors from `tickets/0263`
- `spec/REQUIREMENTS.md` R7 — the per-lane requirement, not this
- the golden fixture work in `tickets/0029`, if it has landed

## Actions

1. Build the cross-lingual probe: EN and FR queries whose relevant answers are
   Vietnamese, plus the other R7 languages the tracker names (German, Greek,
   Russian) as far as the corpus supports them.
2. Run it per candidate at the deployed dtype, on the vectors the CPU arm
   produced.
3. Report per-language-pair, not as one aggregate. A model that carries FR→VI and
   drops EN→EL is a different finding from one that is uniformly mediocre.
4. Report the monolingual lane figure beside the cross-lingual one, so R7 and R29
   are separable in the result.
5. Coordinate with `0037`: hand it the measurement, cite this ticket from there,
   and do not duplicate its requirement text in either direction.

## Test

- A discriminating control: a query whose answer set is in the query's own
  language must score high, and a deliberately unrelated pair must score low.
  Without both, a null result cannot distinguish "no cross-lingual ability" from
  "the probe cannot see it".
- The probe is asserted to run against dtype-matched vectors, per `0265`.

## Verification

- [ ] Per-language-pair figures, not one aggregate
- [ ] The monolingual lane is reported beside the cross-lingual one
- [ ] The positive and negative controls both fired before any figure is quoted
- [ ] `0037` cites this measurement; this ticket states no requirement

## Invariants

- Requirement text belongs to `0037`; this ticket measures
- Corpus languages that are absent are recorded as untestable here, not as a
  zero score
- Every figure declared in `bench/check_figures.py`

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Cross-lingual probe built, with its controls
- [ ] Run per surviving candidate at the deployed dtype
- [ ] Per-pair results committed and declared
- [ ] `0037` updated with a pointer to the evidence, its proposal untouched
